The discussion revolved around the Bangladesh Climate Development Partnership (BCDP), which aims to enhance coherence and synergy in climate governance to overcome the country's climate finance deficit. The platform is established with a high-powered Board and four Working Groups focused on mobilising external and internal financing, building institutional capacity, and project readiness. Key features include a whole-of-society approach that integrates government, private sectors, civil society, and academia, promoting innovative funding mechanisms such as green bonds. The goal is to ensure rapid implementation of climate actions and sustainability. BCDP is positioned as a mechanism for coherent governance, although its long-term effectiveness in addressing climate challenges remains uncertain.
